<!--
  The launcher icon: THE ROUND — the world's one conserved quantity, drawn.

  Microcosm's deepest rule is that matter is never created and never lost here; it only changes
  hands. So the mark is one circle broken into three unequal arcs, in the colours the core's
  bucket table gives the three hands it passes through (frame.rs SPECIES_RGB):

      alga        Solara   #46D68C   the mineral taken up
      grazer      Cilio    #D7A6E8   the alga eaten
      decomposer  Bacillus #9EA868   the mineral released again

  The gaps are the handovers, and the pale speck sitting in the widest of them is the mineral
  itself, mid-flight from the decomposer back to the alga. It is deliberately NOT at the centre:
  a coloured ring around a centred mark reads as an eye, which cost this design three rounds
  (docs/icon-concepts/README.md).

  No amber anywhere. Rule 7 gives amber to the player's hand alone, so it may not appear in the
  world's own imagery — which is what this icon is.

  Geometry, in the adaptive icon's 108-unit canvas: ring radius 25.5 about (54,54), stroke
  weights 10/9.2/8.4 so the outer edge stands at 30.5 of the 33-unit safe circle, with the
  spans carried over from the chosen concept (docs/icon-concepts/chosen.svg). IconTest measures
  that reach on every build rather than trusting this comment.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:aapt="http://schemas.android.com/aapt"
    android:width="108dp" android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108" android:viewportHeight="108">

  <path android:strokeColor="#FF46D68C" android:strokeWidth="10" android:strokeLineCap="round" android:fillColor="#00000000"
      android:pathData="M75.14,39.74A25.5,25.5 0 0 1 61.03,78.51"/>
  <path android:strokeColor="#FFD7A6E8" android:strokeWidth="9.2" android:strokeLineCap="round" android:fillColor="#00000000"
      android:pathData="M46.12,78.25A25.5,25.5 0 0 1 28.64,51.33"/>
  <path android:strokeColor="#FF9EA868" android:strokeWidth="8.4" android:strokeLineCap="round" android:fillColor="#00000000"
      android:pathData="M36.29,35.66A25.5,25.5 0 0 1 56.67,28.64"/>

  <path android:pathData="M65.77,31.38m-7.5,0a7.5,7.5 0 1 0 15,0a7.5,7.5 0 1 0 -15,0z">
    <aapt:attr name="android:fillColor">
